    "created_at": "2018-12-19T18:43:04Z",
    "updated_at": "2018-12-19T18:43:49Z",
    "body": "You're right; the spec doesn't seem to match at least some browsers here. In my testing:\r\n\r\n- Firefox creates an empty video element with no src attribute (!)\r\n- Chrome creates a video element with a source child, as your OP shows\r\n- Safari creates an empty video element with a src attribute\r\n- Edge creates an audio element... but Edge is moving to Chromium\r\n\r\nSample page used: http://www.hochmuth.com/mp3/Tchaikovsky_Rococo_Var_orch.mp3\r\n\r\nBasically this is kind of a mess. I'd be curious to hear from implementers why they chose these routes differing from the spec.\r\n\r\nSince nobody agrees, I would default to keeping the spec as-is, and trying to get folks to converge. So the best next step would be writing a web platform test and filing appropriate issues on the three non-compliant browsers.",
